dts: h616: disable the video-codec node

Linux 7.4-rc1 adds video-codec@1c0e000 to sun50i-h616.dtsi with an iommus
property and no status, so it is enabled by default. That makes the sun50i
IOMMU translate for every master and the display engine (which uses physical
addresses) page-faults on every frame: backlight on, black screen.
No driver is used for the video engine in armiga, so keep the node disabled.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -185,6 +185,7 @@
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 93 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			iommus = <&iommu 3>, <&iommu 2>;
 			allwinner,sram = <&ve_sram 1>, <&sram_c 1>;
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		syscon: syscon@3000000 {
